-- חוזר הממונה על השכר 2016-1-13 — תשלום מענק חד פעמי לעובדי ההוראה בשירות המדינה (22.2.2016)
-- A one-time grant of 1,000 shekels to teaching employees in the state
-- service: who qualifies (continuous employment 1.9.2015–1.1.2016, and the
-- absences that do not break it), the part-time computation, its nature,
-- when it is paid, and the route for those on unpaid leave.
--
-- Corpus note: the source letters section 13's two items (א, ב); the corpus
-- publishes them as 13.1 and 13.2.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT common

§ `מענק חד פעמי לעובדי ההוראה בשירות המדינה 2016-1-13`

-- akn:hc_1/p1 The letterhead; no rule.
-- akn:hc_1/p2 The letterhead's address line; no rule.
-- akn:hc_1/p3 The Hebrew date; no rule.
-- akn:hc_1/p4 The date, 22.2.2016; no rule.
-- akn:hc_1/p5 The circular's number, הע-2016-1-13; no rule.
-- akn:hc_1/p6 The addressee (the Senior Deputy Accountant-General); no rule.
-- akn:hc_1/p7 The subject line; no rule.
-- akn:hc_1/p8 Background: the understandings of 23.12.2015 on the principles of a framework agreement still to be signed; no rule.

DECLARE `grant action` IS ONE OF
    `pay the grant` HAS `grant paid` IS A NUMBER

@desc A kind of absence during the qualifying period, as sections 6-13 name them.
DECLARE `absence kind` IS ONE OF
    `maternity leave`                           @desc under section 6 of the Women's Employment Law, 1954, for a woman or (section 9) a man
    `reserve duty`
    `sick leave under 1.25.3`                   @desc sick leave as in paragraph 1.25.3 of the teachers' service regulations, with salary
    `sick leave without salary`
    `paid absence with the employer's approval` @desc for example rest leave or paid training
    `unpaid leave or an absence treated as one` @desc including unpaid leave after the end of maternity leave (section 7)

@desc A teaching employee in the state service, as far as the grant asks about them.
DECLARE `teaching employee for the grant` HAS
    `a teaching employee in the state service`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `employed throughout 1.9.2015 to 1.1.2016 but for absences` IS A BOOLEAN @desc employed as a teaching employee in the state service through the qualifying period, the absences below aside
    `absences in the qualifying period`               IS A LIST OF `absence kind`
    `full salaried months in a row, 1.9.2015 to 30.6.2016` IS A NUMBER @desc the longest run of whole months, from 1.9.2015 to 30.6.2016, for which salary was due (section 13א(1))
    `and at least one salaried day more`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `any salary due from 1.12.2014 to 30.11.2015`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `months employed from 1.12.2014 to 30.11.2015`    IS A NUMBER
    `average position over the months employed, 1.12.2014 to 30.11.2015` IS A NUMBER @desc the representative monthly average share of a full position over the months actually employed in that period (1 = full)
    `average position from 1.12.2015 to 30.11.2016`   IS A NUMBER

§§ `Preamble — the grant`

-- Under the collective agreement of 17.9.2013 on negotiating the
-- framework agreement's cost for teaching employees, a one-time grant of
-- "1,000 shekels only" is agreed for teaching employees in the state
-- service.
@ref akn:hc_1/p9
`the grant for a full position` MEANS 1000

§§ `1 The qualifying period`

-- 1: a teaching employee in the state service employed continuously from
-- 1.9.2015 to 1.1.2016 ("the qualifying period") gets the grant.
-- 6, 9: maternity leave does not break the continuity (a woman's, or a
-- man's under the Women's Employment Law). 8: the circular's other
-- conditions apply to them too. 10: reserve duty does not break it.
-- 11: sick leave as in 1.25.3 does not break it. 12: paid absence with
-- the employer's approval does not break it.
-- F-2016-02-22_sachar_2016-1-13_maanak-hora-d: section 11 also speaks of
-- "sick leave without salary", which section 13 takes as unpaid leave. The
-- reading adopted sends it to section 13.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_1 akn:hc_1__para_6 akn:hc_1__para_8 akn:hc_1__para_9 akn:hc_1__para_10 akn:hc_1__para_11 akn:hc_1__para_12
GIVEN k IS AN `absence kind`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `leaves the continuity unbroken` k IF
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `maternity leave` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `reserve duty` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `sick leave under 1.25.3` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `paid absence with the employer's approval` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `sick leave without salary` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `unpaid leave or an absence treated as one` THEN FALSE

-- 6 ¶2: the length of maternity leave under the Women's Employment Law is,
-- as a rule, 26 weeks, unless extended as its section 6 details.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_6/p2
`maternity leave in weeks, as a rule` MEANS 26

-- 13 (heading) and 13א: unpaid leave, or an absence treated as unpaid
-- leave, including sick leave without pay, in all or part of the
-- qualifying period, takes the route of 13א. 7: the maternity rule does
-- not cover unpaid leave after maternity leave; it takes "the stated in
-- sub-section – below" (F-2016-02-22_sachar_2016-1-13_maanak-hora-a: the
-- number is blank; read as section 13).
@ref akn:hc_1__para_7 akn:hc_1__para_13 akn:hc_1__para_13__subpara_1
GIVEN t IS A `teaching employee for the grant`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `takes the unpaid-leave route` t IF
    any (GIVEN k YIELD NOT `leaves the continuity unbroken` k) (t's `absences in the qualifying period`)

`the sub-section section 7 names` MEANS ""

GIVEN t IS A `teaching employee for the grant`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `qualifies under section 1` t IF
        t's `a teaching employee in the state service`
    AND t's `employed throughout 1.9.2015 to 1.1.2016 but for absences`
    AND all (GIVEN k YIELD `leaves the continuity unbroken` k) (t's `absences in the qualifying period`)

-- 13א(1): on the unpaid-leave route, the teacher qualifies if, from
-- 1.9.2015 to 30.6.2016, salary was due for 4 full months of work and at
-- least one more day, in a row, full-time or part-time.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_13__subpara_1__cls_1
GIVEN t IS A `teaching employee for the grant`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `qualifies under section 13` t IF
        t's `a teaching employee in the state service`
    AND (    t's `full salaried months in a row, 1.9.2015 to 30.6.2016` AT LEAST 5
          OR (t's `full salaried months in a row, 1.9.2015 to 30.6.2016` AT LEAST 4 AND t's `and at least one salaried day more`))

GIVEN t IS A `teaching employee for the grant`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `qualifies for the grant` t IF
    IF `takes the unpaid-leave route` t
    THEN `qualifies under section 13` t
    ELSE `qualifies under section 1` t

§§ `2 The part-time computation`

-- 2: the 1,000 is for a full position; the grant is proportional to the
-- teacher's position (a representative monthly average) relative to a full
-- position, over 1.12.2014–30.11.2015. 2 ¶2: a part-timer employed in only
-- part of that period, but continuously in the qualifying period, is
-- averaged over the period actually employed. 13א(2): on the unpaid-leave
-- route, the period of 1.12.2014–30.11.2015 actually employed; 13א(3): if
-- no salary at all was due in it, 1.12.2015–30.11.2016.
-- F-2016-02-22_sachar_2016-1-13_maanak-hora-b: a FULL-time teacher employed
-- in only part of 1.12.2014–30.11.2015 is not in 2 ¶2; the reading adopted
-- averages over the months employed for every teacher.
-- F-2016-02-22_sachar_2016-1-13_maanak-hora-e: a position above full; the
-- reading adopted caps the grant at 1,000.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2 akn:hc_1__para_2/p2 akn:hc_1__para_13__subpara_1__cls_2 akn:hc_1__para_13__subpara_1__cls_3
GIVEN t IS A `teaching employee for the grant`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the position the grant is computed on` t IS
    IF `takes the unpaid-leave route` t AND NOT t's `any salary due from 1.12.2014 to 30.11.2015`
    THEN t's `average position from 1.12.2015 to 30.11.2016`
    ELSE t's `average position over the months employed, 1.12.2014 to 30.11.2015`

@export default The one-time grant (in shekels) the circular gives a teaching employee
GIVEN t IS A `teaching employee for the grant` @desc the teacher
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the one-time grant` t IS
    IF `qualifies for the grant` t
    THEN `the grant for a full position` TIMES min (`the position the grant is computed on` t) 1
    ELSE 0

-- The other reading of section 2 for a full-timer employed in only part of
-- the period: the monthly average taken over all twelve months of it.
GIVEN t IS A `teaching employee for the grant`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the grant averaged over the whole twelve months` t IS
    `the grant for a full position`
    TIMES min ((t's `average position over the months employed, 1.12.2014 to 30.11.2015`
                TIMES t's `months employed from 1.12.2014 to 30.11.2015`)
               DIVIDED BY 12) 1

-- The other reading of section 2 for a position above full: proportional,
-- uncapped.
GIVEN t IS A `teaching employee for the grant`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the grant uncapped` t IS
    `the grant for a full position` TIMES `the position the grant is computed on` t

§§ `3-5 The grant's nature`

-- 3: not salary for any purpose; not counted for severance pay or for the
-- hourly value of extra work (overtime, substitute hours, school activity
-- hours); no provident-fund contributions (study fund, pension fund,
-- managers' insurance). 4: not counted when topping up to the minimum wage
-- under the Minimum Wage Law, 1987. 5: it does not change the salary base
-- of the integrated salary tables.
DECLARE `use of the grant` IS ONE OF
    `salary for any purpose`
    `severance pay`
    `the hourly value of extra work`
    `provident-fund contributions`
    `topping up to the minimum wage`
    `the salary base of the integrated tables`

@ref akn:hc_1__para_3 akn:hc_1__para_4 akn:hc_1__para_5
GIVEN u IS A `use of the grant`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the grant counts for` u IF
    FALSE

§§ `1, 6, 11, 13 When it is paid`

-- Time is counted in salary months from February 2016 (0): March 2016 is 1,
-- June 2016 is 4, July 2016 is 5.
-- 1: in the February 2016 salary (paid in March) and no later than the
-- March 2016 salary (paid in April). 6: a teacher on maternity leave: in
-- the first salary after her return and no later than the next. 13א(4): on
-- the unpaid-leave route, in the June 2016 salary (paid in July) and no
-- later than the July 2016 salary (printed "paid in August 2017"; the
-- July salary is paid in August 2016).
-- F-2016-02-22_sachar_2016-1-13_maanak-hora-c: 13א(3)'s period runs to
-- 30.11.2016, after this deadline.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_1 akn:hc_1__para_6 akn:hc_1__para_13__subpara_1__cls_4
GIVEN t IS A `teaching employee for the grant`, `salary month of return from leave` IS A NUMBER @desc for a teacher away on maternity leave at February 2016: the first salary month after the return, counted from February 2016; 0 for any other teacher
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the last salary month for the grant` t `salary month of return from leave` IS
    IF `takes the unpaid-leave route` t THEN 5
    ELSE max 1 (`salary month of return from leave` PLUS 1)

@ref akn:hc_1__para_1 akn:hc_1__para_6 akn:hc_1__para_13__subpara_1__cls_4
GIVEN t IS A `teaching employee for the grant`, `salary month of return from leave` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `grant action`
DECIDE `the employer pays the grant` t `salary month of return from leave` IS
    IF `the one-time grant` t GREATER THAN 0
    THEN PARTY `the employer`
         MUST  `pay the grant` paid
               PROVIDED paid AT LEAST `the one-time grant` t
         WITHIN `the last salary month for the grant` t `salary month of return from leave`
         LEST  BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "2016-1-13: the one-time grant was not paid by the last salary month the circular allows"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- 13ב: the circular is coordinated with the Teachers' Union, which accepts
-- it; the grant will form part of the collective agreement with the union,
-- if a framework agreement with the New General Histadrut is signed.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_13__subpara_2
GIVEN `a framework agreement with the Histadrut is signed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the grant forms part of the union's collective agreement` `a framework agreement with the Histadrut is signed` IF
    `a framework agreement with the Histadrut is signed`

-- akn:conclusions The sign-off (the Wage Controller), the copy to the Civil Service Commissioner, the internal number and the letterhead's footer; no rule.

§§ `Examples`

`a full-time teacher all year` MEANS
    `teaching employee for the grant` WITH
        `a teaching employee in the state service`        IS TRUE
        `employed throughout 1.9.2015 to 1.1.2016 but for absences` IS TRUE
        `absences in the qualifying period`               IS LIST `reserve duty`
        `full salaried months in a row, 1.9.2015 to 30.6.2016` IS 10
        `and at least one salaried day more`              IS FALSE
        `any salary due from 1.12.2014 to 30.11.2015`     IS TRUE
        `months employed from 1.12.2014 to 30.11.2015`    IS 12
        `average position over the months employed, 1.12.2014 to 30.11.2015` IS 1
        `average position from 1.12.2015 to 30.11.2016`   IS 1

`a teacher at 75% on maternity leave` MEANS
    `teaching employee for the grant` WITH
        `a teaching employee in the state service`        IS TRUE
        `employed throughout 1.9.2015 to 1.1.2016 but for absences` IS TRUE
        `absences in the qualifying period`               IS LIST `maternity leave`
        `full salaried months in a row, 1.9.2015 to 30.6.2016` IS 2
        `and at least one salaried day more`              IS TRUE
        `any salary due from 1.12.2014 to 30.11.2015`     IS TRUE
        `months employed from 1.12.2014 to 30.11.2015`    IS 12
        `average position over the months employed, 1.12.2014 to 30.11.2015` IS 0.75
        `average position from 1.12.2015 to 30.11.2016`   IS 0.75

`a teacher on unpaid leave after four months and a day` MEANS
    `teaching employee for the grant` WITH
        `a teaching employee in the state service`        IS TRUE
        `employed throughout 1.9.2015 to 1.1.2016 but for absences` IS TRUE
        `absences in the qualifying period`               IS LIST `unpaid leave or an absence treated as one`
        `full salaried months in a row, 1.9.2015 to 30.6.2016` IS 4
        `and at least one salaried day more`              IS TRUE
        `any salary due from 1.12.2014 to 30.11.2015`     IS TRUE
        `months employed from 1.12.2014 to 30.11.2015`    IS 12
        `average position over the months employed, 1.12.2014 to 30.11.2015` IS 0.5
        `average position from 1.12.2015 to 30.11.2016`   IS 0.5

`a teacher on unpaid leave after four months` MEANS
    `teaching employee for the grant` WITH
        `a teaching employee in the state service`        IS TRUE
        `employed throughout 1.9.2015 to 1.1.2016 but for absences` IS TRUE
        `absences in the qualifying period`               IS LIST `unpaid leave or an absence treated as one`
        `full salaried months in a row, 1.9.2015 to 30.6.2016` IS 4
        `and at least one salaried day more`              IS FALSE
        `any salary due from 1.12.2014 to 30.11.2015`     IS TRUE
        `months employed from 1.12.2014 to 30.11.2015`    IS 12
        `average position over the months employed, 1.12.2014 to 30.11.2015` IS 1
        `average position from 1.12.2015 to 30.11.2016`   IS 1

`a teacher who left in December 2015` MEANS
    `teaching employee for the grant` WITH
        `a teaching employee in the state service`        IS TRUE
        `employed throughout 1.9.2015 to 1.1.2016 but for absences` IS FALSE
        `absences in the qualifying period`               IS LIST `reserve duty`
        `full salaried months in a row, 1.9.2015 to 30.6.2016` IS 3
        `and at least one salaried day more`              IS TRUE
        `any salary due from 1.12.2014 to 30.11.2015`     IS TRUE
        `months employed from 1.12.2014 to 30.11.2015`    IS 12
        `average position over the months employed, 1.12.2014 to 30.11.2015` IS 1
        `average position from 1.12.2015 to 30.11.2016`   IS 0

#ASSERT `the one-time grant` `a full-time teacher all year` EQUALS 1000
#ASSERT `the one-time grant` `a teacher at 75% on maternity leave` EQUALS 750
#ASSERT `the one-time grant` `a teacher on unpaid leave after four months and a day` EQUALS 500
#ASSERT `the one-time grant` `a teacher on unpaid leave after four months` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the one-time grant` `a teacher who left in December 2015` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the last salary month for the grant` `a full-time teacher all year` 0 EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the last salary month for the grant` `a teacher at 75% on maternity leave` 3 EQUALS 4
#ASSERT `the last salary month for the grant` `a teacher on unpaid leave after four months and a day` 0 EQUALS 5
#ASSERT NOT `the grant counts for` `severance pay`
-- The qualifying period, 1.9.2015 to 1.1.2016, is itself four months and
-- one day: 13א(1)'s threshold is the length of section 1's period.
#ASSERT `qualifies under section 13` `a teacher on unpaid leave after four months and a day`

#TRACE `the employer pays the grant` `a full-time teacher all year` 0 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `pay the grant` 1000 AT 1
#TRACE `the employer pays the grant` `a teacher on unpaid leave after four months and a day` 0 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `pay the grant` 500 AT 6

§§ `Findings`

-- F-2016-02-22_sachar_2016-1-13_maanak-hora-a.
`section 7 sends to a sub-section it does not number` MEANS
    `the sub-section section 7 names` EQUALS ""
#ASSERT `section 7 sends to a sub-section it does not number`

-- F-2016-02-22_sachar_2016-1-13_maanak-hora-b: a full-time teacher who
-- joined on 1.9.2015 was employed three months of 1.12.2014–30.11.2015.
`a full-time teacher who joined on 1.9.2015` MEANS
    `teaching employee for the grant` WITH
        `a teaching employee in the state service`        IS TRUE
        `employed throughout 1.9.2015 to 1.1.2016 but for absences` IS TRUE
        `absences in the qualifying period`               IS LIST `reserve duty`
        `full salaried months in a row, 1.9.2015 to 30.6.2016` IS 10
        `and at least one salaried day more`              IS FALSE
        `any salary due from 1.12.2014 to 30.11.2015`     IS TRUE
        `months employed from 1.12.2014 to 30.11.2015`    IS 3
        `average position over the months employed, 1.12.2014 to 30.11.2015` IS 1
        `average position from 1.12.2015 to 30.11.2016`   IS 1

`the two readings of section 2 differ for a full-timer employed part of the period` MEANS
        `the one-time grant` `a full-time teacher who joined on 1.9.2015` EQUALS 1000
    AND `the grant averaged over the whole twelve months` `a full-time teacher who joined on 1.9.2015` EQUALS 250
#ASSERT `the two readings of section 2 differ for a full-timer employed part of the period`

-- F-2016-02-22_sachar_2016-1-13_maanak-hora-c: the latest payment is the
-- July 2016 salary, paid in August 2016; 13א(3)'s period ends on
-- 30.11.2016, three months later. Months counted from February 2016.
`the end of 13א(3)'s period, in months from February 2016` MEANS 9
`the end of 13א(4)'s deadline, in months from February 2016` MEANS 5

`13א(3) measures the grant over a period that ends after 13א(4) pays it` MEANS
    `the end of 13א(3)'s period, in months from February 2016` GREATER THAN `the end of 13א(4)'s deadline, in months from February 2016`
#ASSERT `13א(3) measures the grant over a period that ends after 13א(4) pays it`

-- F-2016-02-22_sachar_2016-1-13_maanak-hora-d: a teacher salaried in
-- September 2015 and then on sick leave without salary to 30.6.2016.
`a teacher on unpaid sick leave from October 2015` MEANS
    `teaching employee for the grant` WITH
        `a teaching employee in the state service`        IS TRUE
        `employed throughout 1.9.2015 to 1.1.2016 but for absences` IS TRUE
        `absences in the qualifying period`               IS LIST `sick leave without salary`
        `full salaried months in a row, 1.9.2015 to 30.6.2016` IS 1
        `and at least one salaried day more`              IS FALSE
        `any salary due from 1.12.2014 to 30.11.2015`     IS TRUE
        `months employed from 1.12.2014 to 30.11.2015`    IS 12
        `average position over the months employed, 1.12.2014 to 30.11.2015` IS 1
        `average position from 1.12.2015 to 30.11.2016`   IS 0

-- Section 11 alone: sick leave does not break the continuity, and a teacher
-- on sick leave without salary is paid on return.
GIVEN t IS A `teaching employee for the grant`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `qualifies by section 11's words` t IF
        t's `a teaching employee in the state service`
    AND t's `employed throughout 1.9.2015 to 1.1.2016 but for absences`

`sections 11 and 13 disagree on unpaid sick leave` MEANS
        `qualifies by section 11's words` `a teacher on unpaid sick leave from October 2015`
    AND NOT `qualifies for the grant` `a teacher on unpaid sick leave from October 2015`
#ASSERT `sections 11 and 13 disagree on unpaid sick leave`

-- F-2016-02-22_sachar_2016-1-13_maanak-hora-e: a teacher at 120%.
`a teacher at 120%` MEANS
    `teaching employee for the grant` WITH
        `a teaching employee in the state service`        IS TRUE
        `employed throughout 1.9.2015 to 1.1.2016 but for absences` IS TRUE
        `absences in the qualifying period`               IS LIST `reserve duty`
        `full salaried months in a row, 1.9.2015 to 30.6.2016` IS 10
        `and at least one salaried day more`              IS FALSE
        `any salary due from 1.12.2014 to 30.11.2015`     IS TRUE
        `months employed from 1.12.2014 to 30.11.2015`    IS 12
        `average position over the months employed, 1.12.2014 to 30.11.2015` IS 1.2
        `average position from 1.12.2015 to 30.11.2016`   IS 1.2

`the two readings of section 2 differ above a full position` MEANS
        `the one-time grant` `a teacher at 120%` EQUALS 1000
    AND `the grant uncapped` `a teacher at 120%` EQUALS 1200
#ASSERT `the two readings of section 2 differ above a full position`
